{"name":"Lynx","hex":"#604d47","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lynx","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Felidae – lynxes."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A faint spring constellation of the northern sky. It lies north of the constellation Cancer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lynx"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lynx","blocks":[{"text":"A lynx is any of the four extant species within the medium-sized wild cat genus Lynx. The name originated in Middle English via Latin from the Greek word lynx, derived from the Indo-European root *leuk-, in reference to the luminescence of its reflective eyes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Lynx_heads_collage.jpg/330px-Lynx_heads_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynx","wikidata":"Q677014"},{"title":"Lynx (Rheinmetall armoured fighting vehicle)","blocks":[{"text":"The Lynx is a German armoured fighting vehicle developed by Rheinmetall. The Lynx, configured as a KF31 infantry fighting vehicle (IFV), was unveiled at the Eurosatory defence exhibition on 14 June 2016. The KF41 variant was unveiled at the Eurosatory defence exhibition on 12 June 2018."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Hungarian_Lynx_KF-41.jpg/330px-Hungarian_Lynx_KF-41.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lynx_(Rheinmetall_armoured_fighting_vehicle)","wikidata":"Q24885889"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Lynx_range.png/500px-Lynx_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Lynx_range.png/1280px-Lynx_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wik